   "source": [
    "EDA on microbiome data from the Johnson et al. 2019 research"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e7339cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Gut Microbiome Data Profiling\n",
    "\n",
    "In this step, we loaded the gut microbiome abundance table (`microbiome.csv`) generated from the Johnson et al. 2019 dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "We performed an initial profiling of the dataset to better understand its structure and characteristics before preprocessing and filtering.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What we examined\n",
    "- Dataset dimensions\n",
    "- Number of microbial features (taxa/species)\n",
    "- Number of samples\n",
    "- First rows of the abundance table\n",
    "- Descriptive statistics for abundance values\n",
    "\n",
    "### Results\n",
    "- The dataset contains:\n",
    "  - **223 microbial features**\n",
    "  - **483 fecal samples**\n",
    "- Rows represent microbial taxa/species.\n",
    "- Columns represent individual microbiome samples.\n",
    "- The abundance values are highly variable across samples, with many low values and zeros, which is common in microbiome datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key observations\n",
    "- Some bacterial species are highly abundant in specific samples.\n",
    "- Many taxa appear at very low abundance levels.\n",
    "- The dataset is expected to be sparse, meaning many entries contain zeros due to absent or rare microbes.\n",
    "\n",
    "This profiling step provides the foundation for the next stages:\n",
    "1. Low-prevalence feature filtering\n",
    "2. Sparsity analysis\n",
    "3. Data preprocessing for downstream microbiome analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2e0306c9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Analyzing Sparsity and Feature Prevalence "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1004,
   "id": "817d71cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Total values in dataset: 107709\n",
      "Number of zero values: 9467\n",
      "Sparsity: 8.79%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate sparsity (percentage of zeros)\n",
    "\n",
    "total_values = microbiome.size\n",
    "zero_values = (microbiome == 0).sum().sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "sparsity = (zero_values / total_values) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Total values in dataset:\", total_values)\n",
    "print(\"Number of zero values:\", zero_values)\n",
    "print(f\"Sparsity: {sparsity:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1005,
   "id": "d3f61800",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "count   223.0000\n",
      "mean      0.9121\n",
      "std       0.1456\n",
      "min       0.2712\n",
      "25%       0.9110\n",
      "50%       0.9731\n",
      "75%       0.9948\n",
      "max       1.0000\n",
      "dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
