       "k__Bacteria;p__Bacteroidetes;c__Bacteroidia;o__Bacteroidales;f__Bacteroidaceae;g__Bacteroides;s__Bacteroides uniformis            1.0000\n",
       "k__Bacteria;p__Bacteroidetes;c__Bacteroidia;o__Bacteroidales;f__Prevotellaceae;g__Prevotella;s__Prevotella copri                  0.9110\n",
       "k__Bacteria;p__Bacteroidetes;c__Bacteroidia;o__Bacteroidales;f__Rikenellaceae;g__Alistipes;s__Alistipes putredinis                0.9938\n",
       "dtype: float64"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Prevalence of each microbial feature\n",
    "# (fraction of samples where feature appears)\n",
    "\n",
    "prevalence = (microbiome > 0).sum(axis=1) / microbiome.shape[1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(prevalence.describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show first prevalence values\n",
    "display(prevalence.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7dbafa82",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sparsity and Prevalence Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "In this step, we analyzed the sparsity and prevalence of the gut microbiome abundance table.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Sparsity Analysis\n",
    "We calculated the percentage of zero values in the dataset to measure sparsity.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Results\n",
    "- Total values in the dataset: **107,709**\n",
    "- Zero values: **9,467**\n",
    "- Dataset sparsity: **8.79%**\n",
    "\n",
    "This indicates that most microbial features are present in many samples, while a smaller portion of the matrix contains absent microbes (zeros).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Prevalence Analysis\n",
    "We then calculated the prevalence of each microbial feature, defined as the fraction of samples in which a feature appears.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key observations\n",
    "- The average prevalence across taxa is very high (~0.91).\n",
    "- Many microbial species appear in nearly all samples.\n",
    "- Some taxa are less common and appear only in a subset of participants.\n",
    "- The minimum prevalence observed was approximately **27%** of samples.\n",
    "\n",
    "These results suggest that the dataset is relatively dense compared to many microbiome datasets, but still contains lower-prevalence taxa that may be filtered in the next preprocessing stage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "333ca40d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Filtering Low-Prevalence Microbial Features"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1006,
   "id": "7d26c075",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Original shape: (223, 483)\n",
      "Filtered shape: (223, 483)\n",
      "Removed features: 0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Filter low-prevalence microbial features\n",
    "\n",
    "threshold = 0.10   # keep taxa appearing in at least 10% of samples\n",
    "\n",
    "filtered_microbiome = microbiome.loc[prevalence >= threshold]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Original shape:\", microbiome.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Filtered shape:\", filtered_microbiome.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Removed features:\", microbiome.shape[0] - filtered_microbiome.shape[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1007,
   "id": "243cff00",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Filtered microbiome dataset saved.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "filtered_microbiome.to_csv(DATA_DIR / \"microbiome_filtered.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Filtered microbiome dataset saved.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1008,
   "id": "d6d6e011",
   "metadata": {},
