   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. Statistical Feature Screening"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0c0b9b76",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To complement the literature-based feature selection, we screened all numeric nutritional variables using three statistical methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Pearson correlation\n",
    "2. Spearman correlation\n",
    "3. Random Forest feature importance\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal was to check whether any nutritional variable shows a stronger relationship with microbiome-related outcomes than the biologically selected features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "72eced47",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Merged shape: (475, 135)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "nutrition[\"study_day_clean\"] = (\n",
    "    nutrition[\"StudyDayNo\"]\n",
    "    .astype(str)\n",
    "    .str.replace(\"Day.\", \"\", regex=False)\n",
    "    .astype(int)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "merged_df = pd.merge(\n",
    "    nutrition,\n",
    "    fme,\n",
    "    left_on=[\"UserName\", \"study_day_clean\"],\n",
    "    right_on=[\"participant_id\", \"study_day\"],\n",
    "    how=\"inner\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Merged shape:\", merged_df.shape)"
   ]
  },
