  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9893ce6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4.7 Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "Statistical screening identified several nutritional variables associated with microbiome outcomes.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, the strongest predictors were not necessarily the classical nutritional variables selected for modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "The final feature set was therefore determined primarily by biological evidence and supported by statistical validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ff070e72",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Modeling the Relationship Between Nutrition and Microbiome Stability"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "33e2979c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In this section, we build a Random Forest Regression model to investigate the relationship between nutritional intake and microbiome stability.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model uses selected nutritional and participant-related features:\n",
    "\n",
    "- KCAL\n",
    "- PROT\n",
    "- TFAT\n",
    "- CARB\n",
    "- FIBE\n",
    "- Age\n",
    "- BMI\n",
    "\n",
    "The target variable is **fme_score_daily**, which represents daily microbiome stability.\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to evaluate whether dietary and participant characteristics can explain variations in microbiome stability and identify the most influential factors."
   ]
  },
